window.docContents[252].resolve({"/Tier-2___-definitions/Symbolic___Specifications___/Symbolic.Specifications.Security.Binary/#file-Symbolic___Specifications___Security___Binary":{"contents":"Paper › Symbolic/Specifications/Security › Binary.leanTier 2 · definitions\n\nTier 2 · definitions used by the symbolic proof 3 headline theorems depend on it 47 of 93 lines trusted source ↗trust banner in the header: B1, trusted: the statement; the closure computes B2 for the symbolic proofRead the definitions shown. Only the declarations that the headline statements use are shown, with the namespace, section, open and variable commands needed to read them. The collapsed runs are theorems, which Lean checks, and definitions that no headline statement uses.\n\n\n\nBinary Security Statement for libsignal-cliTrusted: the statement.States the top-level security theorem SignalSessionSecure bytes for the ARM64 ELF binary implementing PQXDH, SPQR, and the Triple Ratchet, via the run-parametric property SignalSessionSecureFor Agree R.\n\n\n\ndef SignalSessionSecureForL43–66 ↗#Protocol security over run relation R and primitive-agreement predicate Agree from initDirs: for every valid interp, agreeing W, and well-formed r, there exist opaque semantics S such that every guarded, coin-fresh trace evs is either explained (Explains) and satisfies AllSecurityQueriesHoldOnHwTrace, or has an explained prefix evs₁ satisfying AllSecurityQueriesHoldOnHwTrace whose next run event hits NextEventCollides.\n\ndef SignalSessionSecureL68–76 ↗#Binary security and no-fault progress of ELF image bytes: parses bytes, resolves the 18 panic and 5 SampleNTT addresses from .symtab (resolveCliElfAddrs), and asserts CliElfProgress elf addrs and SignalSessionSecureFor HooksMatchPlaced (elfRel elf addrs).\n\ndef SignalSessionSecureRealL78–91 ↗#Binary security and no-fault progress of ELF image bytes at the real primitives: the real primitives obey the symbolic laws (RealPrimsAdmissible); bytes parses and its 18 panic and 5 SampleNTT addresses resolve from .symtab (resolveCliElfAddrs); progress holds (CliElfProgressReal); and SignalSessionSecureFor holds on guarded, coin-fresh traces (CliTraces with ValidCall / InputsFor / LeaksFrom, InvertsGuarded, and CoinsFresh) over elfRelReal elf addrs (no RealHooksAgreeOnInput filter) for every extern interpretation agreeing with realCliHooks (RealPrimsMatch).\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"Symbolic/Specifications/Security/Binary.lean","id":"/Tier-2___-definitions/Symbolic___Specifications___/Symbolic.Specifications.Security.Binary/#file-Symbolic___Specifications___Security___Binary"}});